  "notes": "Cryogenic microwave-cavity light-shining-through-wall (LSW) experiment for hidden-sector (dark) photons. Headline LSW bound: chi < 1.7e-7 at m_gamma' = 53 ueV (5.3e-5 eV); exclusion range in Fig.5 spans frequencies 240 MHz to 24 GHz. This LSW limit is independent of DM density. The same paper ALSO reports separate cold-dark-matter haloscope limits at 53 ueV assuming rho ~ 0.3 GeV/cm^3: chi < 6.14e-14 (homogeneous field, cos^2 theta=0.0025) and chi < 5.32e-15 (inhomogeneous, <cos^2 theta>=1/3). If the CDM result is desired instead, use those values with dm_density=0.3. Only the single explicit LSW point was extractable from text; full Fig.5 curve not tabulated. | vector-trace candidate: chiV2_cropped.pdf colour (0.0, 0.0, 0.0), 197 pts (selected among 3) | selector: vector_trace over text (quality (1, 1, 1, 1, 3.5, 0, 0.85, 197))",
